---
name: cluster-health
description: Quick health snapshot of the k3s Pi cluster + critical AWS resources. Covers SSH/runner status, k3s pods/deployments, Grafana/Keycloak/Lambda reachability, cert expiry. Identifies whether an issue is k3s-side or cloud-side without needing to drill in.
triggers: when the user mentions "is the cluster ok", "k3s health", "Pi runner offline", "cluster status", "deploy stuck", "is grafana up", "is keycloak up", "everything green?", "what's broken"
---

# Cluster Health Snapshot

## One-shot check (run all in parallel)

```bash
echo "=== AWS Lambda (cloud) ==="
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" --max-time 5 https://cloudless.gr/api/health

echo "=== k3s ingress (Pi) ==="
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" --max-time 5 -k -H "Host: cloudless.gr" https://192.168.1.128/api/health

echo "=== Keycloak ==="
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "HTTP %{http_code}\n" --max-time 5 https://auth.cloudless.gr/api/health || echo "Use OIDC discovery:"
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "OIDC discovery: %{http_code}\n" --max-time 5 https://auth.cloudless.gr/realms/master/.well-known/openid-configuration

echo "=== Grafana ==="
curl -s --max-time 5 https://grafana.cloudless.gr/api/health | python3 -m json.tool

echo "=== Pi node SSH ==="
nc -z -w3 192.168.1.128 22 2>&1 && echo "omv-main: OK" || echo "omv-main: REFUSED"
nc -z -w3 192.168.1.130 22 2>&1 && echo "omv-ha:   OK" || echo "omv-ha:   REFUSED"

echo "=== GH self-hosted runners ==="
gh api repos/Themis128/cloudless.gr/actions/runners --jq '.runners[] | "\(.name): \(.status) (busy=\(.busy))"'
```

## Component-specific deep dives

### k3s pods (need SSH or Portainer)

```bash
# Via SSH (if working):
ssh omv@192.168.1.128 'kubectl get pods -A --field-selector status.phase!=Running'

# Via Portainer (if SSH dead) — see `keycloak-ops` skill for the pattern
# Portainer URL: http://192.168.1.128:9000
# Auth: admin / [Portainer password — same as Cognito]
```

### omv runner is offline

The `omv` GH Actions runner is a systemd service `actions.runner.Themis128-cloudless.gr.omv.service` on the Pi. If it's offline:

1. Check SSH first — `nc -z -w3 192.168.1.128 22`
2. If SSH is up, restart via systemctl: `ssh omv@192.168.1.128 'sudo systemctl restart actions.runner.*'`
3. If SSH is down, use Portainer to launch a privileged container that chroots to /host and starts the runsvc.sh manually:

```bash
# Pattern: launch alpine container with /host mount, run nsenter into host PID
# Full recipe in tools/keycloak-cli/keycloak.sh (search for "runner-fix")
```

### Grafana password

Stored in SSM:
```bash
aws ssm get-parameter --name /cloudless/production/GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD \
  --with-decryption --output text --query Parameter.Value
```

Username: `admin`. Login URL: `https://grafana.cloudless.gr/login`

### Pi TLS cert expiry

```bash
echo | openssl s_client -servername cloudless.gr -connect cloudless.gr:443 2>/dev/null \
  | openssl x509 -noout -dates
```

## Common state combinations

| Lambda | k3s | Keycloak | Diagnosis |
|---|---|---|---|
| 200 | 200 | 200 | All healthy |
| 500 | 500 | 200 | Likely Keycloak token verification failing → check Lambda env (AUTH_SECRET, KEYCLOAK_ISSUER) |
| 200 | TIMEOUT | 200 | Pi failover triggered or DNS routing odd |
| 200 | 200 | DOWN | Keycloak pod or postgres down — affects /admin login but public site OK |
| 502 | n/a | n/a | CloudFront couldn't reach origin — check Lambda logs |

## Workflow status (CI/deploys)

```bash
gh run list --repo Themis128/cloudless.gr --limit 15 --json workflowName,conclusion,status \
  | python3 -c "
import sys,json
runs = json.load(sys.stdin)
seen = {}
for r in runs:
    wf = r['workflowName']
    if wf not in seen: seen[wf] = r
for wf,r in sorted(seen.items()):
    icon = '✓' if r['conclusion']=='success' else ('…' if r['status'] in ('in_progress','queued') else '✗')
    print(f'{icon}  {wf}')
"
```
